---
import ContentPage from '../../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import Entry from '../../components/Entry.astro';
import ChipGroups from '../../components/ChipGroups.astro';
import { credentials, papers, profiles, quantumBlog, repos } from '../../data/links';

const skills = [
	{ label: 'Frameworks & libraries', items: ['PyTorch', 'TensorFlow', 'NumPy', 'Pandas'] },
	{
		label: 'ML workflow tools',
		items: ['MLflow', 'Optuna', 'TensorBoard', 'Unity ML-Agents'],
	},
	{ label: 'Environments', items: ['Python', 'Jupyter Notebook', 'Google Colab'] },
];

// Each concept links to the project below that shows it.
const concepts = [
	{ label: 'Reinforcement learning', href: '#spider' },
	{ label: 'Graph neural networks', href: '#upfd' },
	{ label: 'Text encoders', href: '#upfd' },
	{ label: 'Binary classification', href: '#upfd' },
	{ label: 'Hyperparameter optimization', href: '#upfd' },
	{ label: 'Experiment tracking and MLOps', href: '#upfd' },
	{ label: 'Model training, validation and evaluation', href: '#upfd' },
	{ label: 'Implementing published research', href: '#upfd' },
];
---

<ContentPage
	title="Machine Learning"
	eyebrow="Portfolio"
	intro="Research-driven machine learning work, from graph neural networks to reinforcement learning agents."
>
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			During my B.S. in Computer Science, with a minor in mathematics, at Illinois State University, I worked on three
			machine learning research projects with faculty. Each one meant learning a technique from the research literature and
			building it myself. The projects covered graph neural networks for materials science and for detecting
			misinformation, and reinforcement learning for a simulated agent.
		</p>
	</div>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Skills</h2>
		<ChipGroups groups={skills} />
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Concepts</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">Each one links to the project that shows it.</p>
		<ul class="jump-nav">
			{
				concepts.map((c) => (
					<li>
						<a href={c.href}>{c.label}</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Research projects</h2>
		<div class="entry-list">
			<Entry
				id="upfd"
				title="UPFD: Fake News Detection"
				meta="Jan – May 2025"
				subtitle="IT 299 Independent Honors Study, ISU"
				tags={['PyTorch', 'Graph neural networks (GNNs)', 'MLflow', 'Optuna']}
				links={[
					{ label: 'Code', href: repos.upfd },
					{ label: 'Paper', href: papers.upfd },
				]}
			>
				<p>
					Rebuilt the User Preference-Aware Fake News Detection model from a published research paper. It classifies news
					tweets as factual or non-factual using graph neural networks and text encoders, drawing on both the tweet’s content
					and the history of the users who shared it. Training, validation and tuning were automated with MLflow and Optuna.
				</p>
			</Entry>
			<Entry
				id="spider"
				title="Reinforcement Learning: Virtual Spider Agent"
				meta="Jan – May 2023"
				subtitle="MAT 268 Undergraduate Research in Mathematics, ISU"
				tags={['Reinforcement learning', 'Unity ML-Agents', 'C#']}
				links={[{ label: 'Poster', href: papers.spiderPoster }]}
			>
				<p>
					With Joseph Wittrock, trained a virtual spider agent in Unity to follow a moving target without falling over.
					Presented the poster at the ISU Research Symposium.
				</p>
			</Entry>
			<Entry id="stress" title="Predicting Stress Forces in Materials" subtitle="ISU faculty research" tags={['Graph neural networks (GNNs)', 'PyTorch']}>
				<p>Used graph neural networks to predict stress forces in materials.</p>
			</Entry>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Related work</h2>
		<div class="entry-list two-up">
			<Entry title="Parallel Dijkstra’s Algorithm" subtitle="IT 388" links={[{ label: 'GitHub', href: repos.dijkstra }]}>
				<p>MPI and OpenMP versions benchmarked on the Expanse supercomputer: high-performance computing experience.</p>
			</Entry>
			<Entry title="Simplicial Complex Graphing" links={[{ label: 'GitHub', href: repos.simplicial }]}>
				<p>Graph theory and 3D rendering in Python.</p>
			</Entry>
			<Entry title="Representing Quantum Circuits" links={quantumBlog}>
				<p>A three-part blog series covering the linear algebra behind quantum circuits.</p>
			</Entry>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Credentials</h2>
		<div class="list-card card">
			<ul class="plain-list">
				<li>
					Mathematics for Machine Learning Specialization (Imperial College London) ·{' '}
					<a href={credentials.mathForMl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Credential</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					Python for Data Science, AI &amp; Development (IBM) ·{' '}
					<a href={credentials.pythonDataScience} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Credential</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					Tools for Data Science (IBM) ·{' '}
					<a href={credentials.toolsDataScience} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Credential</a>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="cta card">
		<p>Want to talk about ML?</p>
		<ul class="jump-nav">
			<li><a href={profiles.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact me on LinkedIn</a></li>
			<li><a href={profiles.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View code on GitHub</a></li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</ContentPage>
